WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.640
Let’s say you really need
to find reliable information

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.840
about the best diet for
high blood pressure,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.000
or heart disease,
or diabetes.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.360
Where do you go?

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.920
Do you go to a website
sponsored by Big Pharma

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.720
that wants to sell you
pills to fix your problem?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.760
Or, do you want
to treat the cause?

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.280
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.800
with the latest peer-
reviewed research

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.840
on the best ways to eat
healthy and live longer.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.920
They don’t sell this kind
of meth in a back alley.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.840
In today’s story, we
look at the ill effects

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.520
of an excess of methionine,
an amino acid that can cause

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.200
cancerous tumors to grow
and our lifespan to shrink.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.720
This recent review,
noting that vegan diets,

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.160
in part because they tend to be
naturally low in methionine,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.560
may prove to be a useful
nutritional strategy

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.080
in cancer
growth control,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.320
also looked at methionine restriction
and life-span extension.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.400
It seems that the less methionine
there is in body tissues,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.960
the longer different
animals tend to live.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.120
But what are the possible
implications for humans?

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.560
I've talked before about the
free radical theory of aging,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.120
this concept that aging
can be thought of

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.440
as the oxidation
of our bodies

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.160
just like rust is the
oxidation of metal,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.560
and methionine is thought to
have a "pro-oxidant effect."

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.960
So the thinking is that
lower methionine intake

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.440
leads to less free
radical production—

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.760
the so-called reactive
oxygen species,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.800
which slows the rate
of DNA damage,

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.520
which then would slow the
rate of DNA mutation,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.120
slowing the rate of
aging and disease,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.560
thereby potentially
increasing our lifespan.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.720
There are three ways to
lower methionine intake,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.560
caloric restriction—they call
it dietary restriction here,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.880
meaning like you cut your
intake of food in half,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.040
for example only eating
every other day.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.240
That would lower your
methionine intake...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.640
Or, because methionine is found

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.240
concentrated in
certain proteins,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.040
you could practice protein
restriction across the board,

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.600
eating a relatively
protein deficient diet.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.320
Or the third option is
to eat enough food,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.120
eat enough protein, but
just eat plant protein,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.840
because they are relatively
low in methionine.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.680
Caloric restriction is hard,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.000
because you walk around
starving all the time.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.320
Something like
every-other-day eating

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.640
is never likely to
gain much popularity

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.120
as a pro-longevity
strategy for humans,

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.120
so it may be
more feasible

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.440
to achieve moderate
methionine restriction,

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.520
in light of the fact
that plant-based diets

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.320
tend to be relatively
low in this amino acid.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.160
As we've seen, plant products
tend to be lower

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.400
in methionine than
animal products.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.360
Yes, protein restriction
across the board

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.520
can be performed to avoid the
hunger of caloric restriction,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.040
but again, methionine restriction
could also be performed

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.040
emphasizing low-methionine,
high quality

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.720
vegetable sources
of protein.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.360
Among foods containing
plant proteins,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.640
legumes are especially rich
in essential amino acids,

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.000
offering excellent substitutes
for proteins of animal origin.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.240
The fact that beans have
comparatively low methionine

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.120
has been classically
considered a disadvantage.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.480
But given the capacity
of methionine restriction

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.680
to decrease the rate of
free radical generation

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.040
in internal organs,

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.720
to lower markers
of chronic disease,

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.520
and to increase
maximum longevity

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.880
ironically converts such a “disadvantage”
into a strong advantage

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.240
and fits well with the
important role of beans

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.960
in healthy diets like the
traditional Mediterranean diet.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.920
Interestingly, soy protein is also
especially poor in methionine,

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.440
and it is widely considered
that soy-containing foods

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.360
have healthy effects
in human beings.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.560
Now, on a population level

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.120
folks could benefit from just
lowering their protein intake.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:55.840
Period!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.240
"The mean intake of proteins
(and thus methionine)

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.280
of Western human populations
is much higher than needed.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.720
Therefore, decreasing such
levels has a great potential

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.040
to lower tissue
oxidative stress

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.120
and to increase healthy
life span in humans

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.120
while avoiding the possible undesirable
effects of caloric restriction."

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:15.600
First thing we can
recommend is just decreasing

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.080
the intake of protein,
that has a large potential

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.680
to bring about
health benefits,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.960
but then we can lower
methionine even further

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.040
eating a plant-based diet.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.040
The reason plant-based diets

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.960
are so protective
is not known.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.080
Yes, vegetables contain
thousands of phytochemicals,

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.040
but separately investigating
their possible protective roles

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.640
will be an impossible task.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.200
The idea that the
protective effect

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.160
is not due to any of the
individual plant food components,

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.000
but to a synergic “combined effect”
is gaining acceptance.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.560
However, based on
the relationship

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.200
of excess dietary methionine
with toxicity

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.480
to major vital organs and its
likely mechanism of action

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.800
through increase in free
radical generation,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.080
the possibility exists that
the protective effects

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.760
of plant-based
diets can be due,

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.800
at least in part, to their
lower methionine content.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.680
This is not
a new idea.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.560
It was proposed
back in 2009,

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.440
but is only now gaining
increasing acceptance

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.000
in more mainstream
scientific circles.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.880
The idea that "The low-methionine
content of vegan diets

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:26.480
may make methionine restriction feasible
as a life extension strategy."

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.640
In our next story, we learn
how plant-based diets

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.680
may prove to be a
useful nutrition strategy

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.840
because these diets are
naturally lower in methionine.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.640
In designing an antibiotic,

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.240
you wouldn't create a drug
that destroyed DNA, for example,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.520
because that's something that both
humans and bacteria share in common.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.360
It would kill the
bacteria, all right,

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.240
but it might kill us too.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.960
So, many antibiotics work by
attacking the bacterial cell wall,

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.040
something bacteria
have that we don't.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.760
Antifungals can attack the
unique cell walls of fungus.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.520
Pesticides can work by attacking
the special exoskeleton of insects.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.680
But fighting cancer is harder,

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.440
because cancer cells
are our own cells.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.800
So, fighting cancer comes down
to trying to find and exploit

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.120
differences between cancer
cells and normal cells.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.040
Forty years ago, a landmark
paper was published

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.000
showing for the first time
that many human cancers

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.160
have what's called absolute
methionine dependency,

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.120
meaning you can grow normal
cells in a petri dish

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.080
without given them the
amino acid methionine—

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.200
normal cells thrive,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.080
but without methionine,
cancer cells die.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.960
Normal breast cells, for example,

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.120
grow no matter what,
with or without,

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.320
but here's leukemia cells—

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.480
they need that extra
added methionine

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.400
to grow or they just flat-line.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.520
What does cancer do
with the methionine?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.800
Tumors generate gaseous sulphur-
containing compounds with it,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.840
that specially trained diagnostic
dogs can actually pick up.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.000
There are mole sniffing dogs
that can pick out skin cancer.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.000
There are breath-sniffing dogs

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.840
that can pick out people
with lung cancer.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.840
Pee-sniffing dogs that can
diagnose bladder cancer and,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.400
yes - you guessed it.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.800
Fart-sniffing dogs for
colorectal cancer.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:32.000
Doctors can now bring
their lab to the lab…

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.160
Gives a whole new meaning
to the term "pet scan."

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.840
Anyway, methionine dependency

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.440
is not just present in cancer
cell lines in a petri dish,

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.720
Fresh tumors taken from patients
show that many cancers

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.040
appear to have
biochemical defects

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.760
that makes them
methionine dependent,

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.560
including some tumors
of the colon, breast,

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.080
ovary, prostate, and skin.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.560
Chemo companies are
fighting to be the first

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.600
to come out with a methionine-
depleting drug,

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:08.880
but since methionine is
sourced mainly from food

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:12.720
a better strategy may be
to lower methionine levels

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.320
by lowering methionine intake,

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.800
eliminating high methionine foods,
for cancer growth control.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:26.000
Here's the thinking:
look, smoking cessation,

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.360
consumption of diets rich in plants,
and other lifestyle measures

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.160
can prevent the
majority of cancers.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.720
Unfortunately, people don't
do them, and as a result,

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.400
each year hundreds of thousands of
Americans develop metastatic cancer.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.120
Chemotherapy cures only a few
types of metastatic cancer.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.080
Unfortunately, the vast majority
of common metastatic cancers,

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.280
like breast, prostate, colon,
and lung are lethal.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.560
We therefore desperately need novel treatment
strategies for metastatic cancer,

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:59.920
and dietary methionine restriction
may be one such strategy.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.960
So, where is methionine found?

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.520
Particularly, chicken and fish,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.400
milk, red meat and eggs have less,

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.400
but if you really want to stick
with lower methionine foods,

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.560
fruits, nuts, veggies,
grains, and beans.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.520
In other words, methionine
restriction may be achieved

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:30.160
using a predominantly vegan diet.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.800
So, why isn't every
oncologist doing this?

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:39.520
"Despite many promising preclinical and
clinical studies in recent years,

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.200
dietary methionine restriction
and other dietary approaches

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.000
to cancer treatment have not yet gained
widespread clinical application.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:51.440
Most clinicians and investigators
are probably unfamiliar

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:55.280
with nutritional approaches to cancer"...
(ah...that's an understatement).

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.840
"Many others may consider amino acid
restriction as an 'old idea',

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.400
since it has been examined
for several decades.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.160
However, many good ideas remain
latent for decades if not centuries

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.320
before they prove
valuable in the clinic.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.640
With the proper development,
dietary methionine restriction,

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.600
either alone or in combination
with other treatments,

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.414
may prove to have a major impact
on patients with cancer.“

